         custom-columns=":metadata.name" 2>/dev/null || echo                    
         kube-wrong-port-7001)                                                  
         kubectl exec "$POD" -- python3 -c "import urllib.request;              
         print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:7001/').getcode())"     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         6. If the check in step 5 fails, inspect pod status and container logs 
         to find why the server is not serving:                                 
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl get pod kube-wrong-port-7001 -o wide                           
         kubectl describe pod kube-wrong-port-7001                              
         kubectl logs kube-wrong-port-7001 --previous=false                     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         Note: containerPort and EXPOSE are informational; the critical fixes   
         are making the manifest and image consistent with the application      
